OL,3,GNEWSAThe mystery of the saint, the Lord
OL,4,AMayor and the country house
OL,5,
OL,6,FA mysterious underground object could
OL,7,Fconnect a seventh century Anglo Saxon
OL,8,Fprince who became a saint, a Tudor Lord
OL,9,FMayor of London and a Shropshire
OL,10,Fcountry manor.
OL,12,FThe tale has drawn comparisons to a Dan
OL,13,FBrown novel or a historical mystery
OL,14,Fstory, but it is being taken seriously
OL,15,Fby some historians.
OL,17,FIt has also been claimed there is a
OL,18,Fmodern relevance to this saint, even
OL,19,Fthough he lived almost 1,400 years ago.
